# GoodSync

> GoodSync is file synchronization and backup software from Siber Systems, Inc., designed for individuals, businesses, servers, NAS devices, and cloud storage.

GoodSync provides automated file backup and synchronization across computers, mobile devices, servers, NAS devices, removable storage, and cloud services. Jobs can be configured for one-way or two-way operation, with automated, scheduled, real-time, and unattended options. GoodSync supports Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS, Android, and major NAS platforms. It was released in 2006 by Siber Systems, a privately held software company headquartered in Fairfax, Virginia, USA.

Key facts:
- Configurable one-way and two-way jobs for backup and synchronization, with automated, scheduled, real-time, and unattended operation.
- Supports local storage, network shares, FTP, SFTP, WebDAV, Google Drive, OneDrive, SharePoint, Amazon S3, Dropbox, Box, Backblaze B2, Microsoft Azure, and other cloud services.
- GoodSync Connect provides direct peer-to-peer file transfer between computers, servers, NAS devices, and mobile devices without requiring intermediate cloud storage.
- Security features include AES-256 encryption for data in transit and at rest, SSL-secured communication, file version history, and block-level data transfer.
- Business products include GoodSync for Server OS and the web-based GoodSync Control Center for centrally deploying, configuring, and monitoring backup and synchronization jobs.
- Localized pages are available under language prefixes including /de, /es, /fr, /it, /jp, /nl, /ru, /cn, /zh, /br, and /ar.

